# =============================================================================
# .gitignore for the Pekosz Lab Nextstrain repository (PUBLIC on GitHub)
#
# Anything listed here stays on your computer and is never uploaded.
# This file is the first line of defence; the pre-commit and pre-push hooks
# (.githooks/ -> scripts/data_guard.sh) are the second, and they also catch
# data that was renamed, reformatted or moved into a folder not listed here.
# Never force-add an ignored file (git add -f). See the wiki: https://github.com/Pekosz-Lab/nextstrain/wiki/Best-Practices
# =============================================================================

# --- Raw input data: GISAID-licensed and unpublished JHH sequences -----------
# source/ holds JHH_sequences.fasta, JHH_metadata.txt and vaccine.fasta (GISAID).
# GISAID data may not be redistributed; JHH data is private until released on
# GISAID. This is the ONLY folder where raw sequence data may live.
source/

# GISAID-licensed vaccine strains supplied locally for the tutorial
tutorial/vaccine.fasta
tutorial/flusort*

# --- Pipeline working folders (rebuilt by Snakemake every run) -------------------
# Contain copies and derivatives of source/ data, including GISAID vaccine
# sequences, so they are never tracked.
data/
results/
# fludb: the SQLite database built from source/ by the ingest rules
*.db
**.db

# --- Pipeline outputs ------------------------------------------------------------
# Auspice JSONs: inspected by a person, then uploaded to Nextstrain by hand.
auspice/
# Surveillance report: CONFIDENTIAL, internal distribution only.
reports/
# Figures made from build outputs (may show unpublished JHH data).
figures/
# Run logs, benchmarks, provenance and run reports (machine and user details).
.run/
# Timestamped archives of whole runs, including source/ data.
snapshots/
# Snakemake's own state folder.
.snake*/

# --- No data files at the top level of the repository ----------------------------
# Sequences and metadata go in source/; outputs go in results/.
/*.fasta
/*.fa
/*.fna
/*.fas
/*.tsv
/*.csv
/*.xls
/*.xlsx

# --- Notebooks ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Jupyter is not used for new work (marimo or Quarto only), and saved outputs
# can embed data. Existing tracked notebooks are unaffected.
*.ipynb
.ipynb_checkpoints
# marimo session caches
__marimo__/
# Quarto render caches and intermediate files
.quarto/
_freeze/
*.vdoc.r
*.vdoc.python

# --- Operating system and editor clutter ------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
*DS_Store
*DS_Store?
**DS_Store
.DS_Store?
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
Icon?
ehthumbs.db
Thumbs.db
*~
geckodriver.log

# --- Personal settings ------------------------------------------------------------
# Your own agent settings (shared settings live in .claude/settings.json)
.claude/settings.local.json
# Secrets and credentials never belong in the repository
.env

# --- Cluster logs ------------------------------------------------------------------
slurm-*

# --- flusort diagnostics (large, regenerated) --------------------------------------
scripts/flusort/flusort_out
scripts/flusort/flusort_out/blast_output.txt

# --- Work in progress, kept out until complete -------------------------------------
notebooks/reassortment.ipynb
notebooks/tanglegram.ipynb
README2.md
scripts/depreciated